My first ascension with a wizard, and only my second overall! This one 
was rediculously easy, with no conducts. So why a post? Well, even easy 
games of Nethack deserve bragging about, and I am _really_ happy that I 
finally managed to ascend a wizard!

I have been trying for ages to get a wizard far, and it never worked. 
Part of the problem is I don't use Elbereth unless I am an Elf (after 
all, why would others call upon Varda, Elentari? But that's just because 
I'm weird.)

The RNG was truly benevolent. I started out with slow digestion and 
conflict rings, and had the very useful sleep spell to start with. On 
level 1 I found speed boots, and level 3 had a shop with a nice /oW. 
Could it get better? I cheated greatly, as I wished for artifacts I had 
never seen before in my games - you learn a few tricks when you read 
this group.
So Yonder had an easy time with his speed boots, +2 SDSM, helm of 
brilliance, Magicbane and the Eyes of the Overworld. Those are _awesome_.

At one point I saw my first /oD in the posession of a Centaur. Yay for 
the scale mail, thanks for the wand (0:7).
Also a first for me: I kept my kitten Luca alive, found my first 
polymorph in Fort Ludios and that helped, too.

To make a long story somewhat shorter: everything kept going well - 20 
wishes in total, for instance. I haven't kept a complete record due to a 
computer crash and a corrupted text file, but everything was _good_. I 
had a setback when I zapped myself with stone to flesh and lost almost 
all the rings and some wands, but my stash had plenty of duplicates. I 
lost protection when praying at the wrong time, but I was filthy rich 
and just bought new protection at XP level 30.


So, 20 wishes, 24 genocided species, no deaths (but 7 "oLS ready...). 
The only thing I regret is leaving my starting pet Luca on the Plane of 
Earth. I suspect I need the leash next time.

